#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440392 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142780 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "34ea56b4-2066-5aaf-aea9-08515803fc0b" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating an Expression With Parentheses"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48840b8b-45fc-5af4-9eaf-3b0433653b29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48840b8b-45fc-5af4-9eaf-3b0433653b29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440379} :answer-field/id #uuid "5349a1c7-9dd6-5f93-9b66-8b75dd18d825" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440386}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "02df687b-3c38-56ea-bcbb-7b6992abb8b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-134231" :question/problem "Matt and Andrea each bought $6$ ounces of salted peanuts and $4$ ounces of unsalted peanuts. In total, they bought$\\,${{field-1}}\n$\\,$ounces of peanuts." :question/worked-solution "We must write and evaluate an expression representing the total amount of peanuts.\n\nSince each of them bought $6$ ounces of salted peanuts and $4$ ounces of unsalted peanuts, the amount of peanuts they purchased, in ounces, is:\n\n$$\n{{6}_{⏟}}_{\\text{salted peanuts}}+{{4}_{⏟}}_{\\text{unsalted peanuts}}\n$$\n\nSince *each* person purchased this amount of peanuts, and there are $2$ people, we must multiply the amount of peanuts by $2.$ Therefore, the total amount of peanuts is:\n\n$$\n{{(6+4)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{each person}}\\times {{2}_{⏟}}_{\\text{people}}\n$$\n\nTo evaluate the expression, we follow the order of operations with parentheses.\n\nFirst, we perform the operations inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6+4)\\times 2 & =(6+4)\\times 2 \\\\  & =10\\times 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply:\n\n$$\n10\\times 2=20\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440396 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059859 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "85f7df01-47df-5ca6-bdc2-9485017b51bd" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Two-Digit Number by a Two-Digit Number: Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1870102-803f-50cc-8c3b-5afef7cecb4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "504" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1870102-803f-50cc-8c3b-5afef7cecb4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "504" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440382} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9ab1077-8f29-5a4e-a28a-f16902739e34" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440391}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b88dbf04-dd80-54e8-8fde-e4783f40c410" :question/math-academy-id "q-134232" :question/problem "Carla has $12$ packages of almonds, each weighing $42$ ounces. In total, Carla has$\\,${{field-1}}\n$\\,$ounces of almonds." :question/worked-solution "To calculate the total amount of almonds, we need to multiply $12$ by $42.$\n\nSo, we write it this way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  &  &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  &  &  &  & \\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we multiply the ones:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned} \\\\ \\boxed{0}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} & \\,\\, & \\begin{aligned}12\\times 2=24\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we multiply the tens:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{} \\\\ \\boxed{0}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} & \\,\\, & \\begin{aligned}12\\times 40=480\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we add the results:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{} \\\\ \\boxed{0}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,8\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned} & \\,\\, & \\begin{aligned}24+480=504\\end{aligned} \\\\  & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $12\\times 42=504.$\n\nTherefore, Carla has $504$ ounces of almonds in total."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440825 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073842 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "52a1e476-39d5-529d-8632-c5dce93b8ed7" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing When the Hundreds Digit Is Less Than the Divisor"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aa74e7d9-ffc5-5c97-8dc2-f332b10ca40e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440821}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa74e7d9-ffc5-5c97-8dc2-f332b10ca40e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440821} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d8f2ec5-b71f-5d9a-9769-6efad96a0b69" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440822}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ea3c1d03-99bf-511e-b905-8e6710f50246" :question/math-academy-id "q-134233" :question/problem "Carla wants to distribute all the almonds into packages weighing $8$ ounces each. Therefore, Carla will be able to make$\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\,$packages of almonds." :question/worked-solution "We know that Carla has $504$ ounces of almonds in total. Since each package must contain $8$ ounces of almonds, then she will be able to make $504÷8$ packages.\n\nWe start by writing down the question using long division notation:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"2\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{5\\,\\phantom{|}0\\,\\phantom{|}4}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td align=\"left\" width=\"250\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr height=\"20\">\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nNotice that $5$ (the number of hundreds in $504$) is less than the divisor $8.$ Therefore, we should consider both the hundreds and tens:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{5\\,\\phantom{|}0\\,\\phantom{|}4}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$↓$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td align=\"left\" width=\"250\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr height=\"20\">\n<td>Divide: $50÷8=6\\,\\text{R}\\,2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"20\">\n<td>Write over tens: $6$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"25\">\n<td>Multiply: $8\\times 6=48$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"20\">\n<td>Subtract: $50-48=2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"25\">\n<td>Bring down: $4$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nNext, we consider the ones:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#EBF5FB\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\,\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{5\\,\\phantom{|}0\\,\\phantom{|}4}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$8$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$-\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$4$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"15\">$\\boxed{\\text{0}}$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n<td align=\"left\" width=\"250\">\n<table align=\"left\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr height=\"20\">\n<td>Divide: $24÷8=3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"20\">\n<td>Write over ones: $3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"25\">\n<td>Multiply: $8\\times 3=24$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr height=\"20\">\n<td>Subtract: $24-24=0$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nWe get the remainder $0$, so the division is done.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n504÷8=63.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440397 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073698 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b7bb96c-c682-54da-98d7-aa1b6960ee9d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Sum of an Improper Fraction and a Whole Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "186dfbec-40e1-5669-b78b-1a6e666b138c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\frac{8}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440378}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "186dfbec-40e1-5669-b78b-1a6e666b138c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\frac{8}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440378} :answer-field/id #uuid "61d4181d-edef-5c2f-bb3f-ce5a078247b4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440387}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c1e68ffc-d3ca-5167-817a-cc856c132a73" :question/math-academy-id "q-134234" :question/problem "Robert bought $3$ pounds of walnuts while Susan bought $\\frac{17}{9}$ of a pound of walnuts. How many walnuts did they buy together in total? Express your final answer as a mixed number.\n\nThey bought$\\,$ \n{{field-1}}\n$\\,$pounds of walnuts in total." :question/worked-solution "To determine the number of walnuts Robert and Susan bought together in total, we have to calculate the following sum:\n\n$$\n3+\\frac{17}{9}\n$$\n\nTo add $3$ and $\\frac{17}{9},$ we need to express the whole number $3$ as an equivalent fraction with a denominator of $9.$\n\nFirst, we write $3$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{1}\n$$\n\nThen we put this fraction over a denominator of $9$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $9:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 9}{1\\times 9}=\\frac{27}{9}\n$$\n\nSo now, we have to find:\n\n$$\n\\frac{27}{9}+\\frac{17}{9}\n$$\n\nTo add two fractions with like denominators, we add the numerators and keep the denominators the same:\n\n$$\n\\frac{27}{9}+\\frac{17}{9}=\\frac{27+17}{9}=\\frac{44}{9}\n$$\n\nExpressing our answer as a mixed number, we have\n\n$$\n44÷9=4\\,\\text{R}\\,8=4\\,\\frac{8}{9}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, they bought $4\\,\\frac{8}{9}$ pounds of walnuts."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440393 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073826 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5ee87e73-843c-5596-b1f2-341d4e7266f8" :knowledge-point/title "Converting the Final Answer to a Mixed Number: Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f7eeccef-0153-5dbc-86a4-c355fb99fe59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440384}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7eeccef-0153-5dbc-86a4-c355fb99fe59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440384} :answer-field/id #uuid "34368c67-3db4-5d2a-b4a5-7e644a1384c1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440385}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "357eb628-a446-5e21-9526-dabfe7335132" :question/math-academy-id "q-134235" :question/problem "Of the $3$ pounds of walnuts that Robert bought, he gave $\\frac{3}{5}$ pounds to his granddaughter Sophia. As a mixed number, Robert has{{field-1}}\npounds of walnuts remaining." :question/worked-solution "To find out how many walnuts Robert had remaining, we must calculate the difference $3-\\frac{3}{5}.$\n\nTo subtract $\\frac{3}{5}$ from $3,$ we need to express the whole number $3$ as an equivalent fraction with a denominator of $5.$\n\nFirst, we write $3$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{1}\n$$\n\nThen, we put this fraction over a denominator of $5$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 5}{1\\times 5}=\\frac{15}{5}\n$$\n\nSo now, we have to find:\n\n$$\n\\frac{15}{5}-\\frac{3}{5}\n$$\n\nTo subtract two fractions with like denominators, we subtract the numerators and keep the denominators the same. Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\frac{15}{5}-\\frac{3}{5}=\\frac{15-3}{5}=\\frac{12}{5}\n$$\n\nFinally, we convert to a mixed number:\n\n$$\n12÷5=2\\,\\text{R}\\,2=2\\,\\frac{2}{5}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Robert had $2\\,\\frac{2}{5}$ pounds of walnuts remaining."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440395 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198431 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bf381e5b-c6ba-5255-8d6a-797576f71baf" :knowledge-point/title "Comparing Fractions When the Least Common Denominator Equals the Product of Denominators"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f46a10ec-6f4d-59dd-a288-fa100b9f0e3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440383}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f46a10ec-6f4d-59dd-a288-fa100b9f0e3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440383} :answer-field/id #uuid "89dc9221-5a2e-543b-a0cb-442c6540822e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440388} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d48c43c-8024-5436-8502-563ff420ec3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440380}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d48c43c-8024-5436-8502-563ff420ec3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value ">" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440380} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fcd58ca-53e4-51a1-8c9a-e0b485e4a754" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440389}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "994437db-5e6c-52cd-85e4-193a53ab9c7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-134236" :question/problem "After Sophia takes her share of walnuts, Robert's remaining amount of walnuts is{{field-1}}\nthan Susan's amount of walnuts because $2\\,\\frac{2}{5}$\n{{field-2}} $\\frac{17}{9}.$" :question/worked-solution "Robert has $2\\,\\frac{2}{5}$ pounds of walnuts remaining, and Susan has $\\frac{17}{9}$ pounds of walnuts.\n\nWe cannot compare the fractions directly as they don't have a common denominator.\n\nWe can make a common denominator of $5\\times 9=45.$\n\nTo put $2\\,\\frac{2}{5}$ over a denominator of $45,$ we first convert to an improper fraction and then multiply the numerator and denominator by $9:$\n\n$$\n2\\,\\frac{2}{5}=\\frac{12}{5}=\\frac{12\\times 9}{5\\times 9}=\\frac{108}{45}\n$$\n\nTo put $\\frac{17}{9}$ over a denominator of $45,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{17}{9}=\\frac{17\\times 5}{9\\times 5}=\\frac{85}{45}\n$$\n\nWe can now compare the fractions $\\frac{108}{45}$ and $\\frac{85}{45}$ by looking at the numerators only.\n\nSince $108>85,$ the correct statement must be:\n\n$$\n\\frac{108}{45}>\\frac{85}{45}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is\n\n> \"After Sophia takes her walnuts, Robert's remaining amount of walnuts is $>$ than Susan's amount of walnuts because $2\\,\\frac{2}{5}>\\frac{17}{9}.$\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440394 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142796 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "476cf433-d982-5f14-89be-48aea2abaf55" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7401d26c-d5ee-5687-a7b2-679f73e8f3f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440381}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7401d26c-d5ee-5687-a7b2-679f73e8f3f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440381} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7069eb3-7077-523c-883d-c4e8428dace8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440390}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "56c0d0ac-e441-53cb-9b72-c25279d28ac0" :question/math-academy-id "q-134237" :question/problem "Susan ate $\\frac{1}{3}$ of the walnuts that she bought. What **exact** amount of walnuts did she eat?\n\n*Remember that Susan bought $\\frac{17}{9}$ of a pound of walnuts.*\n\nSusan ate$\\,$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\,$pounds of walnuts." :question/worked-solution "We know that Susan has $\\frac{17}{9}$ of a pound of walnuts.\n\nTo calculate the amount that she ate, we need to multiply $\\frac{1}{3}$ by $\\frac{17}{9}.$\n\nTo multiply two fractions, we multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}\\times \\frac{17}{9}=\\frac{1\\times 17}{3\\times 9}=\\frac{17}{27}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, Susan ate $\\frac{17}{27}$ of  a pound of walnuts."}]}
